      "note": "coq-graph-theory packages walks as Path x y with nodes p and writes the edge set of a simple graph as E(G) = sg_edge_set G (in_edges, edgesP); mgraph.walk traverses explicit multigraph edge objects. Neither library has the list or the set of the unordered consecutive pairs of a raw vertex sequence, nor a first-index variant, so GTBase owns seq_edge_list, seq_edge_set and seq_index_edge_set; E(G) is the target of the walk bridges (seq_edge_set_sorted, seq_edge_set_nodes). Digraph P9 dipath_arcs (ordered arc support), D2tur ham_path_edges, the cyclic rot1 extractors (Cycle X9/X24/XE1, Packing X25, GTMisc X216) and U5/X10 colour sequences stay separate. Legacy bodies and per-row certificates: meta/migration_reports/path_edges.md.",
